        ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{x^{6}}{8} - \\frac{7 x^{3}}{4} - 2$ at $\\left(2,-8\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=\\frac{x^{6}}{8} - \\frac{7 x^{3}}{4} - 2$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{3 x^{5}}{4} - \\frac{21 x^{2}}{4}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(2\\right)=\\frac{3 \\left(2\\right)^{5}}{4} - \\frac{21 \\left(2\\right)^{2}}{4}=3\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(3\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-8\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{3}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{3}+\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)+\\left(-8\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{22}{3}\\\\\n\\left(3\\right)y&=-x+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(-24\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(3\\right)y&=-22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $3$ and the constant is $-22$."
      }
    }
  }
